{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ISA",
  "chapter": 44,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet now hear, O Jacob my servant; and Israel, whom I have chosen:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus saith the LORD that made thee, and formed thee from the womb, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " will help thee: Fear not, O Jacob, my servant; and thou, Jesurun, whom I have chosen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I will pour water upon him that is thirsty, and floods upon the dry ground: I will pour my spirit upon thy seed, and my blessing upon thy offspring:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they shall spring up ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " among the grass, as willows by the watercourses.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "One shall say, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD'S; and another shall call ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "himself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by the name of Jacob; and another shall subscribe ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his hand to the LORD, and surname ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "himself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by the name of Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus saith the LORD the King of Israel, and his redeemer the LORD of hosts; I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the first, and I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the last; and besides me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And who, as I, shall call, and shall declare it, and set it in order for me, since I appointed the ancient people? and the things that are coming, and shall come, let them show to them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fear ye not, neither be afraid: have not I told thee from that time, and have declared ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "? ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " even my witnesses. Is there a God besides me? verily ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no God; I know not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They that make a graven image ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all of them vanity; and their delectable things shall not profit; and they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their own witnesses; they see not, nor know; that they may be ashamed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who hath formed a god, or cast a graven image ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is profitable for nothing?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, all his fellows shall be ashamed: and the workmen, they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of men: let them all be assembled, let them stand up; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they shall fear, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they shall be ashamed together.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The smith with the tongs both worketh in the coals, and fashioneth it with hammers, and worketh it with the strength of his arms: yes, he is hungry, and his strength faileth: he drinketh no water, and is faint.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The carpenter stretcheth out ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " rule; he marketh it out with a line; he fitteth it with planes, and he marketh it out with the compass, and maketh it after the figure of a man, according to the beauty of a man; that it may remain in the house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He heweth down cedars for himself, and taketh the cypress and the oak, which he strengtheneth for himself among the trees of the forest: he planteth an ash, and the rain doth nourish ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then shall it be for a man to burn: for he will take of it, and warm himself; indeed he kindleth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and baketh bread; yes, he maketh a god, and worshipeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; he maketh it a graven image, and falleth down to it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He burneth part of it in the fire; with part of it he eateth flesh; he roasteth meat, and is satisfied: yes, he warmeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "himself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and saith, Aha, I am warm, I have seen the fire:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the residue of it he maketh a god, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his graven image: he falleth down to it, and worshipeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and prayeth to it, and saith, Deliver me; for thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my god.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have not known nor understood: for he hath shut their eyes, that they cannot see; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their hearts, that they cannot understand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And none considereth in his heart, neither ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " knowledge nor understanding to say, I have burned part of it in the fire; I have also baked bread upon its coals; I have roasted flesh, and eaten ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": and shall I make the residue of it an abomination? shall I fall down to the stock of a tree?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He feedeth on ashes: a deceived heart hath turned him aside, that he cannot deliver his soul, nor say, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Is there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not a lie in my right hand?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remember these, O Jacob and Israel; for thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my servant: I have formed thee; thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my servant: O Israel, thou shalt not be forgotten by me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have blotted out, as a thick cloud, thy transgressions, and as a cloud, thy sins: return to me; for I have redeemed thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sing, O ye heavens; for the LORD hath done ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": shout, ye lower parts of the earth: break forth into singing, ye mountains, O forest, and every tree therein: for the LORD hath redeemed Jacob, and glorified himself in Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus saith the LORD thy Redeemer, and he that formed thee from the womb, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "I am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD that maketh all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; that stretcheth forth the heavens alone; that spreadeth abroad the earth by myself:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That frustrateth the tokens of the liars, and maketh diviners mad; that turneth wise ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " backward, and maketh their knowledge foolish;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That confirmeth the word of his servant, and performeth the counsel of his messengers; that saith to Jerusalem, Thou shalt be inhabited; and to the cities of Judah, Ye shall be built, and I will raise up her decayed places:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That saith to the deep, Be dry, and I will dry up thy rivers:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.44.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.44.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That saith of Cyrus, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "He is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my shepherd, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall perform all my pleasure: even saying to Jerusalem, Thou shalt be built; and to the temple, Thy foundation shall be laid.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
